# Build context rules for web/Dockerfile, which is the one image built from the
# repo root (bff/ has its own context and its own .dockerignore).
#
# This file does not decide what ends up in a layer: web/Dockerfile copies named
# paths, never `.`, so the COPY lines are the control. This is about what crosses
# into the build at all, which is why .env is the first entry that matters.

.env
.env.*

.git
.gitignore

# Installed and generated trees. node_modules is reinstalled from the lockfile in
# the image, and a host .next built on a different platform would be copied over
# a fresh build for no reason.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/dist
